Z||000000||lowfierogt||05-14-2001||11:06 PM||||How hard is it to take out the rear exhaust manifold on the V6?<P>Thanks<BR> <A HREF="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com" TARGET=_blank>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com</A> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||cadaver||05-14-2001||11:23 PM||||Do you mean REAR or FRONT. Wall either way its just a matter of taking out the bolts. They get hard because the like to get frozen to the head and the y pipe. A little penetrating oil and some heat usually do it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-14-2001||11:24 PM||||I have done the frt manifold on both v6 auto and 4spd.  once you remove the converter there is actually more room to work than you would think.  My auto also had A/C, for that I completely unbolted compressor (leaving refrigerant lines connected) and dropped over to the drivers side.  My manifolds where not cracked but warped-just ground them down and double gasketed the far right port due to warping.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sjp777||05-14-2001||11:40 PM||||It's not breaking the bolts that's the hard part, especially on the one closest to the passenger compartement. They love to break and it is a huge pita to get them out if they do.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||13
Z||000004||lowfierogt||05-14-2001||11:53 PM||||How hard is it to take the deep one out if you have a car host?  And what happens if you break a bolt.  I live in mn and you know how they salt the roads this makes it easy for them to break.  Im on a time crunch.  What do I do.   <BR>The close one gets real red hot also whats that from?  I have one more dumb thing.  How much oil do you put in a 2.8 and whats the oil pressure at idle?<P>thanks for all the good info.<P> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||AkursedX||05-15-2001||12:09 AM||||4.5 quarts with a filter change.  As for oil pressure, when fully warmed up, it sits a little below 1/2way on the guage, i don't know exact numbers though||||reg||1
